[[2047,127,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>It is not possible to order a\nsingle lock barrel or to order barrels simply by using a part code.</p><p>When\nordering barrels, observe the special procedure set out in \n                                                         <a href=\"#/3238539\">5580E</a>\n                                                          .</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Keep handle button (1a) pressed in and remove the key barrel\nretaining clip (1b).</p><p>2. Take out the key barrel (the barrel is part of the button).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018955.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the barrel is undamaged.</p><p>1. Insert the key barrel retaining clip.</p><p>2.  Fit the key barrel (2b) and engage notches (2b) with the retaining\nclip</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018956.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<p>Check that the barrel and the\nlock control mechanism are working properly.</p>"]]